{"metadata":{"taxon":[{"Plain":"Wiki. "},2],"slug":[{"Plain":"Langlands 对偶"},0],"title":[{"Plain":"“Langlands 对偶”"},1]},"content":{"Plain":"\n<p>设 $G$ 为约化代数群, 其 Langlands 对偶 ${^LG}$ 是另一个代数群,</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Given a reductive algebraic group $G$, one constructs its Langlands dual $^LG$ by applying an involution to its root data. Under the Langlands correspondence, <strong>automorphic representations</strong> of the group $G$ (其实是 $G(\\mathbb A_F)$) correspond to <strong>Galois representations</strong> with values in $^LG$ (即同态 $\\mathrm {Gal}(\\overline{F}/F)\\to {^LG}$).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>规范理论中的 Langlands 对偶</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A gauge theory has a coupling constant $g$, which plays the role of the electric charge $e$. The conjectural non-abelian electro-magnetic duality, which has later become known as $S$-duality, has the form $(G, g) \\leftrightarrow (^LG, 1/g)$.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>几何 Langlands 对应</h2>\n<p>[局部几何 Langlands 对应](局部几何 Langlands 对应.md)</p>\n<h2>相关概念</h2>\n<p>[Langlands 纲领](Langlands 纲领.md)</p>\n"}}